Baselines. We evaluate our approach against several baselines spanning different paradigms: (1) constraint-based methods: Fast Causal Inference (FCI) ;

(2) score-based methods: NOTEARS , SDCD (3) FCM-based methods: Dif-fAN (4) pre-training-based methods: AVICI , SEA . We additionally include two fundamental statistical measures as reference points: global Pearson correlation (CORR) and inverse covariance matrix (INVCOV) .

Evaluation metrics. To evaluate causal discovery performance, we adopt four standard metrics for causal structure learning: Structural Hamming Distance (SHD), Mean Average Precision (mAP), Area Under the ROC Curve (AUC), and Orientation Accuracy (OA). To evaluate causal discovery efficiency, we report two metrics: inference time and peak GPU memory.
